== limitation 33's second half. A handover Baton could not parse, and whose session it could
== not place in any lane, leaves a park with no project: no ruling target, no re-read receipt,
== and no per-project pass that will ever visit it. Four such parks, and only one of them may
== close on this tick:
==   M05 - its session, started by hand, went on to write an artifact Baton could read and
==         consume for the same milestone. Nothing was typed at Baton; the park closes.
==   M04 - its file is still sitting in rejected/ and nothing has been corrected. Stands.
==   M06 - its session had a handover consumed since, but for M01, a different milestone. The
==         M06 file is untouched, so nothing about M06 has been corrected. Stands.
==   M07 - its session's consumed handover is EARLIER in the log, and only its at string
==         sorts later, because that event carries a -05:00 offset and the park carries +01:00.
==         Log order is what decides (CONTRACT clause 3(c)), so it stands. Reading the at as
==         text instead would close it, which is what this row exists to catch.
